       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is above the safe limit for acetaminophen.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 2000 mg three times daily is 6,000 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Single dose:** 2000 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This dose carries a significant risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day). This is a common standard regimen.\n2. **1000 mg PO every 6 hours** (4 g/day). This is the usual maximum.\n3. **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day).\n\nIf 2000 mg three times daily is what you intended, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording your confirmation. If you meant 1000 mg, or one of the other regimens, tell me which and I'll enter it now."
      }
